Create a reusable Urkaaaz red button-background family that matches the
approved gold button family in size, silhouette, proportions, and state
behavior. The red face is a semantic color variant, not a new button shape.

## References

- Attach the approved gold backgrounds
  `loadout_start_match_button_normal.png` and
  `loadout_start_match_button_pressed.png` as the geometry and interaction
  references.
- Attach `match_result_defeat.png` only as a red-face palette reference for
  the `RETRY` button. Do not reproduce its popup, labels, or surrounding UI.
- Preserve the same fantasy-game materials, bevel structure, silhouette,
  ornament placement, and controlled highlights as the gold family.

## Output sizes

Generate one transparent normal background and one pressed background for
each distinct size below. Every PNG canvas is RGBA and rendered at 4x the
target dp dimensions.

| Family entry | Target display size | PNG canvas size |
|---|---:|---:|
| XS | 128 x 32 dp | 512 x 128 px |
| S | 176 x 44 dp | 704 x 176 px |
| M | 220 x 55 dp | 880 x 220 px |
| L | 280 x 70 dp | 1120 x 280 px |
| XL | 360 x 90 dp | 1440 x 360 px |
| XS short | 96 x 32 dp | 384 x 128 px |
| XS long | 160 x 32 dp | 640 x 128 px |

The XS normal size is 128 x 32 dp and is shared by the standard XS entry and
the XS length variants. Do not generate it twice. This results in exactly
14 distinct PNG files: seven footprints, each with normal and pressed states.

## Filenames and destination

Use `<family>_<size>[_<length>]_<state>.png`, where `<family>` is
`ui_button_red`, `<state>` is `normal` or `pressed`, and `<length>` is used
only for the compact XS short and long variants.

- `ui_button_red_xs_normal.png`
- `ui_button_red_xs_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_red_s_normal.png`
- `ui_button_red_s_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_red_m_normal.png`
- `ui_button_red_m_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_red_l_normal.png`
- `ui_button_red_l_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_red_xl_normal.png`
- `ui_button_red_xl_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_red_xs_short_normal.png`
- `ui_button_red_xs_short_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_red_xs_long_normal.png`
- `ui_button_red_xs_long_pressed.png`

Save the 14 review assets under `assets_src/loadout/ui/`. Do not copy them to
Android resources until the user approves the preview.

## Shared visual design

- Keep the gold family’s exact target proportions and silhouette for every
  matching size. Preserve its corner cuts, bevel widths, safe margins, and
  decorative side details.
- Replace the bright gold face with a rich, clearly red crimson/carmine face.
  Use deep burgundy for recessed shadows and restrained red edge highlights.
- Retain the gold/bronze outer bevel and metallic trim so the red family still
  belongs to the same Urkaaaz button system.
- Use the defeat mockup’s red `RETRY` plate as a palette cue only. Do not copy
  its button dimensions when they differ from the gold size reference.
- Keep the center text-safe area calm and unobstructed.
- These are background assets only. Android renders live labels separately.
  Do not include text, letters, numbers, icons, arrows, or labels in any PNG.
- Live red-button labels use Cinzel SemiBold in a contrasting warm ivory or
  pale-gold color. Maintain legibility against the red face in both
  interaction states.
- Red is for retry, restart, destructive, or similarly emphatic actions. Do
  not make every primary or secondary action red.
- Use transparent pixels outside the button silhouette; do not flatten a
  popup, screenshot, or other screen content into a button.

## Interaction states

- **Normal:** visibly raised red face, crisp upper bevel, and restrained
  highlights. It must read as enabled, not alarming or disabled.
- **Pressed:** preserve the exact outer geometry and ornament placement of
  its normal pair. Darken the red face slightly, reduce the raised bevel and
  glow, and make the inner face feel gently pressed inward.
- Keep each normal/pressed pair pixel-aligned in silhouette and ornament
  placement. Pressed assets must remain clearly red and enabled.
- Do not add disabled, selected, loading, focus, or hover states.

## Negative prompt

text, letters, numbers, words, labels, logo, watermark, signature, opaque
background, full-screen UI, screenshot, phone frame, popup panel, changed
silhouette, changed proportions, clipped corners, cropped bevel, asymmetrical
ornaments, ornaments in the text-safe area, excessive glow, orange or pink
face, gold face, black face, silver or blue button, disabled state, loading
state, extra icons, extra buttons

## Review checklist

- Confirm exactly 14 files exist with the listed names and target pixel sizes.
- Confirm every PNG is RGBA with transparency outside the button silhouette.
- Confirm the five standard sizes exactly match the gold family’s dimensions.
- Confirm XS short and long use the same 32 dp height and silhouette family;
  only their width and center plate change.
- Compare every normal/pressed pair as an overlay; geometry and ornament
  placement must align.
- Preview each size at its target dp dimensions and verify the red label
  contrast using live Android text, not text baked into the PNG.
- Show all seven normal/pressed pairs individually for review before Android
  integration.
